WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.469
Critical thinking is often needed most when information is incomplete.

00:00:03.469 --> 00:00:05.828
Waiting for perfect certainty can be impossible,

00:00:05.828 --> 00:00:08.523
but acting without enough thought can be costly.

00:00:08.523 --> 00:00:13.240
Decision-making under uncertainty asks how much we know, how much we do not know,

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:17.283
what risks matter, and whether more analysis would meaningfully improve the choice.

00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:19.978
Probability is a practical way to express uncertainty.

00:00:19.978 --> 00:00:24.021
You do not need complex math for the basic habit to help.

00:00:24.021 --> 00:00:28.738
Saying something is possible is less useful than estimating whether it is unlikely, plausible,

00:00:28.738 --> 00:00:30.086
likely, or highly likely.

00:00:30.086 --> 00:00:34.129
That level of clarity helps teams decide whether to gather more evidence,

00:00:34.129 --> 00:00:37.161
add a control, run an experiment, or move forward.

00:00:37.161 --> 00:00:38.172
Tradeoffs are unavoidable.

00:00:38.172 --> 00:00:42.215
A faster decision may preserve momentum but increase the chance of error.

00:00:42.215 --> 00:00:45.584
A slower decision may improve confidence but miss an opportunity.

00:00:45.584 --> 00:00:46.258
Reversibility matters.

00:00:46.258 --> 00:00:49.627
If a choice can be rolled back or tested cheaply,

00:00:49.627 --> 00:00:55.018
it may not need the same level of analysis as a commitment that locks in cost,

00:00:55.018 --> 00:00:56.702
architecture, risk, or public trust.

00:00:56.702 --> 00:01:00.745
Opportunity cost is the value of what is given up when one

00:01:00.745 --> 00:01:02.430
option is chosen over another.

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:05.799
If a team spends its limited time investigating one hypothesis,

00:01:05.799 --> 00:01:07.484
it is not investigating another.

00:01:07.484 --> 00:01:10.179
If an organization chooses a highly customized tool,

00:01:10.179 --> 00:01:12.537
it may give up simplicity or maintainability.

00:01:12.537 --> 00:01:17.591
Critical thinking keeps these costs visible rather than pretending that preferred options have no downside.

00:01:17.591 --> 00:01:19.949
Pre-mortems and decision records are practical tools.

00:01:19.949 --> 00:01:24.329
A pre-mortem imagines a future failure and asks what might have caused it.

00:01:24.329 --> 00:01:27.362
A decision record captures the frame, evidence, assumptions, tradeoffs,

00:01:27.362 --> 00:01:29.046
and reasoning behind a choice.

00:01:29.046 --> 00:01:29.696
Together,

00:01:29.696 --> 00:01:34.100
they help teams act under uncertainty while preserving a trail for review and learning.
